  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 5♣. West's heart lead has created a heart loser for South. There is no reason to duck the opening lead. The ♣A must also be lost. South's only concern is that one opponent has all 4 outstanding trumps.\n\nIf East has 4 clubs, South must play the ♣Q or ♣J on the first round of the suit. South can later take the marked finesse against the ♣10.\n\nIf West has all 4 clubs, South must play the ♣K immediately. West will win the ♣A, cash a heart trick, and exit in diamonds. South has the spot cards to double finesse West out of the ♣10 and ♣8. South will need two hand entries to the closed hand to do this. Only one entry, the ♠K, is readily available.\n\nSouth must risk finessing East for the ♠J to gain an extra hand entry. South plays a club towards dummy. West will force a club honour from North. South can return to the ♠K and finesse again in clubs.\n\nSouth should play West for 4 clubs. West must have the ♣A for his opening bid. He thus cannot be void of clubs.",
